Subject: scryfall_search shows 20 cards a page, each in its newest paper printing

Found in the assistant tool review of the live gateway (2026-10-28):

- A verbose search returned all 73 results (about 37 KB) with no way to ask
  for fewer. scryfall_search now takes limit (default 20, at most 175) and
  page counts pages of that many, read across Scryfall's own 175-card pages.
  The first line says which cards are shown ("Showing 21-40.") and how to get
  the next; a page past the end says how many pages there are.
- Its cards came in Scryfall's default printing (Siege-Gang Lieutenant as
  The List, PLST), while scryfall_named shows the newest printing out on
  paper. A search now uses the same policy through Scryfall's prefer:newest
  with game:paper (unless the query names a game). printing picks another:
  scryfall (Scryfall's own choice), cheapest (prefer:usd-low) or oldest; a
  prefer: term in the query wins. The query is put in parentheses so an "or"
  in it keeps the added terms on the whole query. A line says which
  printings are shown.

tests/test_search_limit_and_printing.py.

Upstream: Kautiontape/mystic-forge at dd82cd1 has none of these. Needs
patches 0001-0015 applied first.
